🛒 Amazon Product Price Prediction

A Machine Learning project that predicts the actual price of Amazon products based on features like discount, rating, rating count, and product category.

---

🚀 Project Overview

This project uses a Random Forest Regression model to estimate the original price of Amazon products using:

- Discounted Price
- Discount Percentage
- Rating
- Rating Count
- Product Category (One-Hot Encoded)

The application is built with a Streamlit frontend and a FastAPI backend to provide real-time price predictions.

---

📊 Dataset

The dataset contains Amazon product information including:

- Product Category
- Discounted Price
- Actual Price (Target Variable)
- Discount Percentage
- Rating
- Rating Count

---

🧠 Machine Learning Workflow

1. Data Cleaning & Preprocessing
2. Handling Missing Values
3. One-Hot Encoding
4. Feature Selection
5. Model Training
6. Model Evaluation
7. Model Deployment

---

🤖 Models Used

- Linear Regression
- Decision Tree Regressor
- KNN Regressor
- Random Forest Regressor
- XGBoost Regressor

---

🏆 Best Model Performance

- Random Forest Regressor
- R² Score: ~95%

---

📦 Tech Stack

- Python 🐍
- Pandas & NumPy
- Scikit-learn
- Random Forest Regressor
- Streamlit (Frontend UI)
- FastAPI (Backend API)
- Joblib (Model Saving)

---

🖥️ Application Features

- Select Product Category
- Enter Discounted Price
- Enter Discount Percentage
- Enter Rating & Rating Count
- Real-Time Price Prediction
- FastAPI REST API Integration

---

⚙️ Installation & Setup

1️⃣ Clone Repository

git clone https://github.com/sayanc889-wq
cd amazon-price-prediction

2️⃣ Install Dependencies

pip install -r requirements.txt

3️⃣ Run FastAPI

uvicorn main:app --reload

4️⃣ Run Streamlit

streamlit run app.py
